# Production high/critical advisories that are knowingly accepted, by package
# name. `checks.sh sec` fails when this list stops matching reality in EITHER
# direction: a new advisory is a finding, and one that disappears means the
# exemption is stale and should be removed.
#
# Every entry is one chain. @prisma/client depends on the prisma CLI, which
# carries tooling and drivers for databases this project never touches, and each
# of those brings its own dependencies. That is the whole reason these appear in
# a --omit=dev audit at all. The only fix npm offers is prisma 7 -> 6, a major
# downgrade of the ORM. Recheck on every Prisma upgrade and delete lines the
# moment they clear.
#
#   prisma, @prisma/config, deepmerge-ts
#       Stack exhaustion merging recursive objects. @prisma/config reads
#       prisma.config.js, a local trusted file, never attacker input.
#
#   mysql2
#       Auth-plugin downgrade and a decompression bomb in the MySQL wire
#       protocol. This application speaks to PostgreSQL through
#       @prisma/adapter-pg and never opens a MySQL connection, so no code path
#       reaches it. The driver ships because the CLI supports every database.
#
#   fast-uri
#       SSRF and host confusion in URI parsing, reached through ajv inside
#       @prisma/dev - Prisma's own development tooling, which is not on this
#       application'''s request path.
@prisma/config
deepmerge-ts
fast-uri
mysql2
prisma
